<v Michael Chabon>"Mrs. Stokes," said Mrs. Gladfelter, coming out of the principal's office. "It's been kind of a long afternoon for Timothy, I'm afraid." "How is Virginia?" said Mrs. Stokes. She still hadn't looked at Timothy. "Oh, she'll be fine," Mr. Buterbaugh said. "Just a little shaken up. We sent her home early. Of course," he added, "Her parents are going to want to speak to you."
<v Michael Chabon>"斯托克斯太太，"格拉德费尔特太太从校长办公室走出来说道。"恐怕对蒂莫西来说，这是一个漫长的下午。""弗吉尼亚怎么样了？"斯托克斯太太说。她依然没有看蒂莫西一眼。"哦，她会没事的，"巴特博恩先生说。"只是有点受惊。我们让她提前回家了。当然，"他补充道，"她的父母想跟您谈谈。"

