00:28:49.050 --> 00:29:20.380
<v Michael Chabon>I shrugged. "Are you going to make him go to special school?" I said. "All right, Paul. Thank you," said Mrs. Gladfelter. "You may go back to class now." "See you later, Timothy," I said. He didn't answer me. He had started to growl again. As I followed the secretary out of the office, I looked back and saw Mr. Buterbaugh, and Mrs. Gladfelter, and poor old Mrs. Stokes standing in a hopeless circle around Timothy.
<v Michael Chabon>我耸了耸肩。"你们要让他去特殊学校吗？"我说。"好了，保罗。谢谢你，"格拉德费尔特太太说。"你现在可以回教室去了。""回头见，蒂莫西，"我说。他没有回答我。他又开始发出低吼声了。我跟着秘书走出办公室时，回过头看到巴特博恩先生、格拉德费尔特太太和可怜的老斯托克斯太太绝望地围成一圈站在蒂莫西身边。

00:29:20.380 --> 00:29:52.440
<v Michael Chabon>I thought for a second, and then I turned back toward them and raised an imaginary rifle to my shoulder. "This is a dart gun," I announced. Everyone looked at me, but I was talking to Timothy now. I was almost, but not quite embarrassed. "It's filled with darts of my special antidote. And I made it stronger than it used to be, and it's going to work this time. And also, there's a tranquilizer mixed in."
<v Michael Chabon>我琢磨了一秒钟，然后转身对着他们，把一把想象中的步枪举到肩头。"这是一把麻醉枪，"我宣布。所有人都看着我，但我现在是在跟蒂莫西说话。我几乎感到有些不好意思，但还没完全不好意思。"里面装满了我的特制解药。而且我把它配得比以前更浓了，这次绝对管用。另外，里面还混了镇静剂。"

00:29:52.440 --> 00:30:17.320
<v Michael Chabon>Timothy looked up and bared his teeth at me. And I took aim right between his eyes. I jerked my hands twice and went "Foop, foop!" Timothy's head snapped back, and his eyelids fluttered. He shook himself all over. He swallowed once, then he held his hands out before him as if wondering at their hairless pallor.
<v Michael Chabon>蒂莫西抬起头，向我龇牙咧嘴。我瞄准了他的双眼之间。我的双手猛地晃了两下，发出了"呼——呼——！"的声音。蒂莫西的头猛地向后一仰，眼皮颤动着。他全身剧烈地抖动了一下。他咽了一口唾沫，然后把双手举在身前，仿佛在端详它们那失去毛发、变得苍白的颜色。

00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:48.920
<v Michael Chabon>"It seems to have worked," he said, his voice cool, and reasonable, and fine. Anyone could see he was still playing his endless game, but all the grown-ups, Mr. Buterbaugh in particular, looked very pleased with both of us. "Thank you very much, Paul," he said. "I'm not Paul," I said. Everybody laughed but Timothy Stokes.
<v Michael Chabon>“看来起作用了，”他说，声音冷静、理智而又悦耳。任谁都能看出他仍在进行他那没完没了的游戏，但所有的大人们，尤其是巴特博恩先生，对我们两个的表现都感到非常满意。“非常感谢你，保罗，”他说。“我不是保罗，”我说。除了蒂莫西·斯托克斯，所有人都笑了。

